ChenDimensionOne.lean adapts the local interval comparisons in
MathlibNt/SieveTheory/Arithmetic/MertensTheorem.lean and the local logarithmic
estimate in AnalyticNumberTheory/Mertens/Basic.lean. The port uses the
project's own prime reciprocal notation and proved Mertens bounds.

For distributions including the Suzuki linear-sieve port, its vendored files
retain their upstream module paths and copyright headers. The local port
adjusts imports and proofs for Lean and Mathlib 4.36. Its
RosserSuzukiUpperInterval.lean adapts
the all-depth argument from
MathlibNt/SieveTheory/LinearSieve/Suzuki/SuzukiUpperRosserAllDepth.lean
to the parameter range starting at s > 1.
